134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 388 0 R
/E (Another of Airbnb's verticals, "Experiences," is an interesting business category sitting inside the core lodging business, allowing both to gather new users and to funnel existing ones into it, to provide a traveller/explorer with literally more "Experiences.")
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 389 0 R
/E (I firstly identified the core user it was made towards. Quite obviously, it was for foreign tourists lodging or using hotel services and then wanting to explore local activities while they are here. I segmented them based on their demographics: one person, a family, or friends travelling. I identified a standard user story and user flow.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E (Then I went to a separate, individualistic segmentation, based on how they broadly book services: "the deliberate planner," "the intuitive planner," and "the impulsive adventurer." During all this, I kept myself very detailed.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 391 0 R
/E (Then I took a real-world example to show how foreigners actually book these services and what exactly they look for, on their website: 1\) first impression, via good-quality pictures and trust building through that; 2\) which then is validated by reviews driven by the people who already used those services; essentially being facilitated by testimonials rather than independent quality work by Airbnb.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
